  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Brief DescriptionThe Joint Programme applies a nuanced, area-based, and conflict-sensitive approach, ensuring that community participation is optimized. This includes targeted efforts for the inclusion of conflict-affected and marginalized groups, such as women, youth, people with disabilities and the elderly.UNJP 2.0 is a collaborative initiative that brings together the combined expertise and capacities of six UN agencies: FAO, UNDP, UNFPA, UN-Habitat, UNICEF, and WFP. The programme aims to</narrative>
